# Gangamata Transport — Mobile App Configuration (Expo / React Native)
# Copy to .env (or .env.local) for local development. Never commit .env.
# IMPORTANT: Never place secrets, API keys, or private tokens in EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables are embedded into client bundle code during build.

# ── API Base URL ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The one backend shared by the driver app and the office web console (NestJS on Render, data in
# Supabase PostgreSQL). This is also the default when the variable is unset, so a development build
# served by Metro talks to the same API as the released APK. Metro only serves the JavaScript bundle;
# it is never the backend — do not point this at localhost, an emulator alias or a LAN address.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://gtransport-7vgf.onrender.com
#
# Metro on a physical phone over Wi-Fi may need your PC's address for the *bundle* only. That is a
# Metro setting, not an API one: put REACT_NATIVE_PACKAGER_HOSTNAME=<your PC's LAN IP> in .env.local.

# ── App Environment ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# development | staging | production (drives non-secret behaviour like logging)
EXPO_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=development

# ── Live Fleet map (Phase 6, office app) ──────────────────────────────────────
# The office Fleet screen draws with native MapLibre (no Mapbox or Google key). What it draws is a
# MapLibre *style* URL: the tile source, fonts and look. Pointing a build at a self-hosted
# OpenStreetMap-derived tile server, or a provider you have a production agreement with, is an
# environment change — no code edit. Any absolute http(s) MapLibre style URL works; mapbox:// does not.
#
# Deliberately unset by default with no built-in map. Without it Fleet says "Map configuration is
# unavailable." and the driver list, details and Open in Google Maps keep working.
#
# It is embedded in the app bundle, so if a provider needs a key it must be a client-safe,
# restricted one. Changing it needs a Metro restart (npx expo start --clear), not a native rebuild.
#
# Local development only: OpenFreeMap serves OpenStreetMap data through a public style with no key.
# Do not use it, or the public openstreetmap.org tile servers, as the production source.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_MAP_STYLE_URL=https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty

# ── Location tracking (Phase 6) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing to configure here on purpose. How often the app reports, how far apart the fixes are and
# how many it may buffer offline all come from the API (GET /locations/tracking-policy), so the
# office can tune tracking without shipping a new build to every driver's phone.
#
# Background location does require a development build rather than Expo Go, because it uses native
# modules: run `npm run android` (or `expo run:android --device`) after installing dependencies.
